<Project>

  <!--
    Ships fl-layout-dump.exe beside the importing project's output.

    It emits the native shared-memory struct layout as JSON, and
    ShmLayoutMirrorTests consumes it to assert that the C# mirrors in
    FrameLedger.Shared match fl_shm.h field for field. That is the mechanism
    CLAUDE.md §Struct mirroring calls the protection for the shm ABI, and until
    2026-08-05 it did not exist: nine files described it in the present tense
    while src/FrameLedger.Shared held only a .csproj.

    WHY THE DUMP AND NOT A TABLE IN THE TEST. A hand-written offset table in C#
    is a SECOND statement of the layout, and two statements of one fact drift —
    which is the defect the whole mirror exists to catch, reintroduced in the
    thing catching it. tools/rules-validate.ps1 makes the same choice for the
    rules bounds: extract the constants from the header, and FAIL rather than
    skip if they cannot be read.

    Imported by exactly one project: FrameLedger.Infrastructure.Tests.

    Unlike FrameLedger.Guard.targets this stages a TOOL, not a shipped artifact.
    It never reaches out/app: nothing in the product runs it, and an executable
    that dumps internal layout has no business in a release.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <FlLayoutDumpDir>$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)build\native\x64-release\tools\fl-layout-dump\</FlLayoutDumpDir>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="$(FlLayoutDumpDir)fl-layout-dump.exe" Condition="Exists('$(FlLayoutDumpDir)fl-layout-dump.exe')">
      <Link>fl-layout-dump.exe</Link>
      <CopyToOutputDirectory>PreserveNewest</CopyToOutputDirectory>
    </None>
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    Warn at BUILD time, fail at TEST time. build.ps1 runs the native build first,
    so by the time this evaluates the exe exists; a hard error here would make
    `dotnet build` on a fresh clone fail for a reason unrelated to managed code.

    The test itself does NOT extend that courtesy: a mirror test that cannot find
    its native input reports FAILED, never "skipped", because "could not look"
    reading as "looked and it matched" is exactly the defect class this
    repository keeps recording.
  -->
  <Target Name="FlWarnOnMissingLayoutDump" AfterTargets="Build"
          Condition="!Exists('$(FlLayoutDumpDir)fl-layout-dump.exe')">
    <Warning Text="fl-layout-dump.exe was not found at $(FlLayoutDumpDir). Run build.ps1 native first; ShmLayoutMirrorTests will fail without it." />
  </Target>

</Project>
